One key observation is that when the pole angle was greater than 0 (indicating the pole was leaning to one side) and its angular velocity was also positive, moving the cart to the right (action 2) seemed to help correct the lean. Conversely, if the pole was leaning to the other side (pole angle < 0), moving the cart to the left (action 1) helped.

