4. For all other scenarios not covered by the above rules, default to cautious adjustments that prioritize maintaining a centered cart with minimal velocity.

By incorporating these lessons learned from my experiences and refining my approach, I aim to develop a more effective strategy for balancing the pole, one that can adapt to a variety of scenarios and maintain stability over longer periods.
